# atomic sandbox replay v1
# M6 bonds, labels, isotopes and Relax on the water preset (Task 10's script): two O-H bonds and
# the label "H2O - water"; select an H (nucleus 1) and make it 2H, and the formula stays H2O;
# Relax settles the geometry and the readout says it converged; still two bonds, still water.
# Honest about the geometry: at the default h = sigma = 0.25 the smeared oxygen makes this
# surface's minimum nearly linear (O-H 2.34 Bohr, about 177 degrees; measured here: O-H 2.338),
# 0.16 Ha below the physical 104.5-degree start (the h2o preset's note) - a resolution artefact,
# so the script checks that the relax converges and the bonds survive, not the angle.
view 1400 900
action smooth-motion false
action preset h2o
wait idle
expect bonds 2
expect molecule 0 H2O
action tool select
t 100 cursor 0.1967989 -0.1277001
t 110 button left down
t 170 button left up
expect selected 1
action isotope 1 2
wait idle
expect isotope 1 2
expect molecule 0 H2O
action relax
wait idle
expect relaxed true
expect bonds 2
expect molecule 0 H2O
expect no-error
